# First run, the same with or without a connection: the first screen behind
# the catalog leads with the books on this device, says what each catalog
# holds, and names no test catalog and no raw address.
tap Back
wait-for On this device
expect Nothing is ready offline yet.
expect Over 70,000 free books whose copyright has run out.
expect-missing OPDS 2.0 Test Catalog
expect-missing https://
clean
shot gutenbird-home
tap On this device
wait-for Open a book in a catalog and tap Read.
clean
shot gutenbird-device-empty
tap Back
wait-for Catalogs
# The daily loop, live from Project Gutenberg. A book opens straight onto its
# own page with no choice of edition to make first. Pride and Prejudice's
# illustrated edition is too large for a reader, so the one without pictures
# is taken and one tap on Read downloads and opens it.
tap Project Gutenberg
wait-for Popular
tap Popular
wait-for All Books
clean
shot gutenbird-popular
# Search is a field the reader's keyboard opens, with the recent searches
# and the switch for every catalog in sight before anything is typed.
tap-id search
wait-for Search every catalog
clean
shot gutenbird-search
tap-id query
wait-for-id kb.enter
clean
shot gutenbird-search-typing
tap Back
wait-for Search every catalog
tap Back
wait-for All Books
tap Pride and Prejudice
wait-for-id read
expect-missing With images
expect-missing No images
expect English
clean
shot gutenbird-book
# Search by typing on the reader's keyboard, and page the results.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for All Books
tap-id search
wait-for Search every catalog
tap-id query
wait-for-id kb.enter
type austen
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for Books: austen
wait-for Emma
clean
shot gutenbird-search-results
tap-id shelf-next
wait-for 2 of
tap-id shelf-back
wait-for 1 of
# A book with several downloads offers them, and its description pages.
tap Emma
wait-for-id read
expect Choose download
maybe-tap-id about-next
wait-idle
maybe-tap-id about-back
wait-idle
tap Choose download
wait-for Each keeps its own reading position
expect no images
clean
shot gutenbird-formats
tap no images
wait-for-id read
clean
shot gutenbird-edition-chosen
# The page should describe the edition that was chosen, not the catalog's
# default one.
expect-missing This edition has images.
